[{"content":"You can call these tools (parameters are JSON Schema; \"required\" lists the required arguments, and \"default\" is the value used when an optional argument is left out):\n\n[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"kube.get_pod_logs\",\n    \"description\": \"Fetch the most recent log lines of one pod's container, optionally from its previous crashed run.\",\n    \"parameters\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"pod\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"Full pod name, exactly as listed, e.g. 'checkout-api-7d9f8-x2kqp'.\"\n        },\n        \"namespace\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"Kubernetes namespace the resource lives in.\",\n          \"default\": \"default\"\n        },\n        \"tail_lines\": {\n          \"type\": \"integer\",\n          \"description\": \"Number of lines to return, counted from the end of the log.\",\n          \"default\": 100\n        },\n        \"previous\": {\n          \"type\": \"boolean\",\n          \"description\": \"Read the log of the previous, terminated container instance.\",\n          \"default\": false\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"pod\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Movies_3_FindMovies\",\n    \"description\": \"Retrieves a list of movies based on the specified director, genre, and cast. The default behavior without parameters is to find a wide range of movies without specific preferences.\",\n    \"parameters\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"directed_by\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"The name of the movie's director. Use 'dontcare' to ignore this filter.\",\n          \"default\": \"dontcare\"\n        },\n        \"genre\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"The genre category of the movie. Use 'dontcare' for no specific genre preference.\",\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"Offbeat\",\n            \"Fantasy\",\n            \"World\",\n            \"Mystery\",\n            \"Thriller\",\n            \"Comedy\",\n            \"Comedy-drama\",\n            \"Horror\",\n            \"Animation\",\n            \"Sci-fi\",\n            \"Cult\",\n            \"Drama\",\n            \"Anime\",\n            \"Family\",\n            \"Action\",\n            \"dontcare\"\n          ],\n          \"default\": \"dontcare\"\n        },\n        \"cast\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"A comma-separated list of actors in the movie. Use 'dontcare' to ignore this filter.\",\n          \"default\": \"dontcare\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": []\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"calendar_event_create\",\n    \"description\": \"Creates a new calendar event for the user and returns the details of the event in JSON format. The event can be a single occurrence or follow a specified recurrence pattern.\",\n    \"parameters\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"start_date\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"The start date of the event in the format 'YYYY-MM-DD'.\"\n        },\n        \"start_time\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"The start time of the event in 24-hour format 'HH:MM'.\"\n        },\n        \"duration\": {\n          \"type\": \"integer\",\n          \"description\": \"The duration of the event in minutes.\"\n        },\n        \"rrule\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"A string specifying the recurrence pattern for repeating events, following the iCalendar (RFC 5545) specification.\",\n          \"default\": \"Does not repeat\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"start_date\",\n        \"start_time\",\n        \"duration\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"kube.restart_deployment\",\n    \"description\": \"Restart every pod of a Kubernetes deployment with a rolling restart, keeping the replica count.\",\n    \"parameters\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"deployment\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"Name of the deployment, exactly as given, e.g. 'checkout-api'.\"\n        },\n        \"namespace\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"Kubernetes namespace the resource lives in.\",\n          \"default\": \"default\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"deployment\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"kube.list_pods\",\n    \"description\": \"List the pods in a namespace with their status, restart counts and owning deployment.\",\n    \"parameters\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"namespace\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"Kubernetes namespace the resource lives in.\",\n          \"default\": \"default\"\n        },\n        \"status\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"Only list pods in this phase.\",\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"Running\",\n            \"Pending\",\n            \"Failed\",\n            \"Succeeded\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"labels\": {\n          \"type\": \"object\",\n          \"description\": \"Only list pods carrying all of these labels.\",\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"app\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"description\": \"Value of the pod's 'app' label.\"\n            },\n            \"tier\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"description\": \"Value of the pod's 'tier' label.\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": []\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": []\n    }\n  }\n]\n\nRequest: List the pods in the prod namespace whose status is Failed.\n\nReply with only a JSON array of the tool calls that fulfil the request, each of the form {\"name\": \"<tool name>\", \"arguments\": {...}}, where \"arguments\" is a JSON object (not a string). When the request needs several calls, list them all. Reply with [] if no tool fits the request, or if the request does not give a value for a required argument: never guess one. Include every required argument. Include an optional argument only if the request asks for a value for it; otherwise leave it out and the tool applies its default. Give each value the type its schema declares: JSON numbers for integer and number, true or false for boolean, and strings for string, copied exactly as written.","role":"user"},{"content":"[{\"name\":\"kube.list_pods\",\"arguments\":{\"namespace\":\"prod\",\"status\":\"Failed\"}}]","role":"assistant"},{"content":"Tool results:\n[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"kube.list_pods\",\n    \"result\": [\n      {\n        \"pod\": \"billing-worker-8586-x17q\",\n        \"deployment\": \"billing-worker\",\n        \"status\": \"Failed\",\n        \"restarts\": 8\n      },\n      {\n        \"pod\": \"search-indexer-9622-x46q\",\n        \"deployment\": \"search-indexer\",\n        \"status\": \"Failed\",\n        \"restarts\": 26\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n]\n\nRequest: Show me the last 50 log lines of the one with the most restarts, from its previous run.\n\nReply as before: only a JSON array of tool calls, or [] if no tool fits or a required value is missing.","role":"user"}]